PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

The stronger-damage experiment is wired correctly.

We doubled the unavailable-cell footprint from eight to sixteen cells, but
did not change how long the damage lasts, how much work arrives, how long
requests live, what the task computes, or how much authority the neural
recruiter has.

The neural recruiter is still blind to the lesion itself.

In the fixed pre-freeze fixture it changes three real recruitment decisions,
while both arms still complete the same 147 correct jobs with no wrong
answers and no expiry.

So the ten fresh worlds can now be created from a frozen implementation.

